    "problem_statement": "Path division operator produces reversed paths\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen using the `/` operator on Path objects, the resulting path segments are being reversed unexpectedly.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom furl import Path\n\n# Basic path division\np = Path()\nresult = p / 'a' / 'b'\nprint(f\"Expected: 'a/b', Got: '{result}'\")\n\n# Path object division\np1 = Path('e')\np2 = Path('f')\nresult = p1 / p2\nprint(f\"Expected: 'e/f', Got: '{result}'\")\n```\n\nThe paths are coming out reversed - 'a/b' becomes 'b/a' and 'e/f' becomes 'f/e'.\n\nAlso noticed that the `/=` operator has similar issues where subsequent operations on the same Path object produce unexpected results due to shallow copying behavior."
  }
